# DTF tier manifest: proxy-download-ledger  (artifact-keeper#4535, #4539, #4551,
# #4267, #4341; all fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + a run-time-filled upstream (upstreams.mock-files:
# a stdlib-python server on a per-slot 172.16.<slot>.0/24 subnet whose files
# the oracle writes over a control API and which counts every request per
# path). The oracle reads proxy_download_statistics, download_statistics and
# proxy_cache_artifacts directly. Every request of a case carries its own
# User-Agent, so a case counts only its own rows; user_agent exists in both
# statistics tables on every image, so the counts are portable to 1.10.0.
#
# THE BUGS
# #4535  Both two-phase virtual resolvers recorded only a HOSTED winner. A
#        virtual download answered by a Remote member (cache hit or upstream
#        fetch) landed in neither download table.
# #4539  proxy_download_statistics was keyed only on proxy_cache_id, ON
#        DELETE CASCADE from the catalog, so evicting or purging a cache entry
#        erased its download history; /admin/downloads listed hosted rows
#        only and /admin/stats total_downloads ignored proxy serves.
# #4551  An object larger than the Remote's quota is streamed without a cache
#        write, but the download recorder still upserted a catalog
#        placeholder, which stayed behind as a "cached" 0-byte entry.
# #4267  A Maven GET through a virtual answered by a hosted member was not
#        counted.
# #4341  An npm tarball GET through a Remote without scan-on-proxy was not
#        counted.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on 1.10.0, GREEN on 1.11.0 and main:
#              #4535 virtual [Remote that 404s, Remote that serves] GET -> one
#                    row under the winning member's (repository_id, path), none
#                    for the losing member, none for a HEAD;
#              #4539 POST cache/invalidate on a downloaded entry -> catalog row
#                    gone, download row kept with proxy_cache_id NULL and its
#                    (repository_id, path); /admin/downloads?source=proxy&
#                    repository_id= lists it (source proxy, artifact_id null,
#                    path) and source=hosted does not; one proxy serve moves
#                    /admin/stats total_downloads and proxy_download_count by 1;
#              #4551 the over-quota Remote has no catalog row at all and its two
#                    download rows carry the (repository_id, path) key;
#              #4267 Maven virtual GET from a hosted member -> one
#                    download_statistics row on the member's artifact, HEAD none;
#              #4341 npm Remote tarball GET -> one row, HEAD none.
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: a direct generic Remote GET serves the
#              upstream bytes and is counted once (HEAD not); a direct hosted
#              Maven GET is counted once (HEAD not); the over-quota object is
#              served in full from upstream on every GET (never cached) and each
#              GET is counted.
#
# NOT GATED HERE (see the PR): the age-gated virtual npm last-known-good
# tarball counted under its member (#4341's second half) needs a held version
# plus a cached older one; the lifecycle-policy eviction path of #4539 (this
# tier evicts through POST cache/invalidate, the same catalog delete).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: ~40 authenticated calls back to back.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the mock upstream is on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-files"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
